  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting of a pastel valley with striped mountains, a blocky city, airships, and round headed creatures on stepped ground.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on wood in four panels, with the panel seams faintly visible as a cross. At the top, triangular mountains in pink, lavender and tan under a pale pink sky with a yellow sun. Two green and yellow airships with lenses and nozzles fly at upper left and centre. A blue lake crosses the middle with a row of outlined blocky buildings on its far shore. The lower half is stepped platforms of flat colour, orange, pink, yellow and green, with round headed figures: a blue horned creature at centre, a purple striped quadruped, a pink winged dragon at right, a cluster of white and blue bottle shaped figures at left, and arcing pipes with red bands that emerge from the water. Colours are soft and matte with thin dark outlines.",
    "impression": "A quieter cousin of the Superland paintings, where the crowd has thinned out and the ground has become terraces. The airships give it a slow, floating feeling, and the little creatures look like they are waiting for something to arrive from the mountains. It reads as a landscape of patient toys.",
